{"bookId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL", "title": "Future Politics", "bookmarks": {"synckey": 1698761889, "updated": [{"bookId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL", "bookmarkId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL_22_57849-58111", "createTime": 1698761889, "range": "57849-58111", "markText": " I said in chapter nine that the digital lifeworld would be thick with power and drenched with politics. If we care about liberty, there must also be a corresponding increase in the ability of the citizenry to hold that power to account.", "colorStyle": 2, "type": 1, "chapterUid": 22}, {"bookId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL", "bookmarkId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL_22_3749-3997", "createTime": 1698593252, "range": "3749-3997", "markText": "One of the curious traits of digital technology, as we’ve seen, is that it can enhance and restrict our freedom at the same time. It frees us to do things that we couldn’t do previously. But it restricts us according to the constraints of the code.", "colorStyle": 2, "type": 1, "chapterUid": 22}], "removed": [], "chapters": [{"title": "11. Freedom and the Tech Firm", "chapterUid": 22, "chapterIdx": 22}], "book": {"bookId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL", "version": 271848388, "format": "epub", "soldout": 0, "bookStatus": 1, "cover": "https://res.weread.qq.com/wrepub/CB_1446KG6MT4Ek6hW6gW38i4yw_parsecover", "title": "Future Politics", "author": "Jamie Susskind", "coverBoxInfo": {"colorsPure": ["#93B0DA", "#98B8DD"]}}}, "reviews": {"reviews": [{"reviewId": "17408780_7Mkpultlf", "review": {"bookId": "CB_0jXFJnFKn3Th6k16ke6Bl9NL", "content": "Why do digital systems become the subject of the topic?", "bookVersion": 271848388, "range": "2641-2887", "abstract": "For the generation now approaching political maturity, the debate will be different: to what extent should our lives be directed and controlled by powerful digital systems—and on what terms? This question is at the heart of Future Politics", "type": 1, "isPrivate": 1, "chapterUid": 8, "reviewId": "